.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-INVITATIONS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-invitations - Discover pending invitations received by you or administered for a team


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team invitations [team] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List pending invitations: the ones addressed to you, or with a team argument the ones
that team has outstanding (owners and admins). Each line shows invitation ID, team, recipient,
state and expiry. Filter with --q (email or ID); the list stops at --limit unless you pass --all.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	show every item, up to 10000

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for invitations

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	show at most this many items (1-200)

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by email or ID


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team invitations
  pb team invitations acme --q ana
  pb team invitations --all --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
